WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:06.770
Black Panther smashed projections with a record-breaking
$235 million four-day total, making it the

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:11.640
fifth largest domestic opening weekend of
all time despite debuting in February, which

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.910
is usually one of the slowest months of the
year.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:18.200
So how did it manage to crush expectations
and take over the cultural consciousness?

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.789
Here's a look at how Black Panther blew everyone
away at the box office.

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.330
Royal reviews

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:28.609
Most films in the Marvel Cinematic Universe
have garnered positive reviews, but Black

00:00:28.609 --> 00:00:32.759
Panther took it to the next level, enjoying
widespread critical acclaim.

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:33.890
How widespread?

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:39.610
The film currently holds a 97% score on Rotten
Tomatoes, making it the best reviewed superhero

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:43.660
film of all time, above even The Dark Knight.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:44.899
Building buzz

00:00:44.899 --> 00:00:49.380
Months before its release, Black Panther started
building incredible word of mouth.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:54.899
The movie's teaser trailer scored 89 million
views in the first 24 hours after its highly-promoted

00:00:54.899 --> 00:01:00.140
debut during Game 4 of the 2017 NBA Finals,
making it one of the most viewed trailers

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.230
ever for any Disney film.

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:06.689
That buzz immediately spilled over onto social
media, with the movie generating more mentions

00:01:06.689 --> 00:01:09.799
on Twitter than the NBA game during which
it debuted.

00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:13.639
This continued throughout the lead-up to the
film, and helped the movie earn second place

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:19.530
on Fandango's survey of the most anticipated
films of 2018 — after only Marvel's Avengers:

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:20.810
Infinity War.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:26.029
Black Panther has since become the most-tweeted
about movie of 2018 — a distinction it achieved

00:01:26.029 --> 00:01:29.049
even before it hit theaters.

00:01:29.049 --> 00:01:30.459
Excited audiences

00:01:30.459 --> 00:01:35.390
Black Panther continued to build on that buzz
when it hit theaters, earning an A+ CinemaScore

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:40.290
from opening night viewers — only the second
Marvel movie to do so, after The Avengers.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:44.939
And many fans lined up to see Black Panther
multiple times, as Fandango reported that

00:01:44.939 --> 00:01:49.619
the movie had a "significantly higher" number
of repeat viewers than any other film during

00:01:49.619 --> 00:01:50.880
its opening weekend.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.090
Dave Hollis, Disney's President of Theatrical
Distribution, said

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:59.489
"It's not like anything we've ever experienced
before, it has taken on its own life.

00:01:59.489 --> 00:02:04.229
The way people are talking about the experience
is that, 'I saw it on Thursday, but I'm coming

00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:07.779
back on Saturday, and might be back on Tuesday.'"

00:02:07.779 --> 00:02:09.939
The #BlackPantherChallenge

00:02:09.939 --> 00:02:12.469
The excitement moved off social media as well.

00:02:12.469 --> 00:02:17.020
Grassroots events have popped up across the
United States surrounding the film, with activists

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:20.319
using the movie as a way to bring their communities
together.

00:02:20.319 --> 00:02:25.500
Philanthropist Frederick Joseph launched the
#BlackPantherChallenge to raise $40,000 to

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:30.459
help kids in Harlem see the film, but the
challenge has since spiraled out even further,

00:02:30.459 --> 00:02:35.209
resulting in over $600,000 raised by a number
of campaigns from celebrities and regular

00:02:35.209 --> 00:02:36.359
people alike.

00:02:36.359 --> 00:02:40.400
The challenge brought more positive buzz and
excitement to the film, while bringing the

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.150
moviegoing community together in support of
a good cause.

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:47.180
"Just being able to like let these kids know
that anything is possible.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.900
You're capable of doing anything if you put
your mind to something you can achieve it."

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:52.930
Big screen representation

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:57.219
Much of the buzz surrounding Black Panther
is thanks to its predominantly black cast,

00:02:57.219 --> 00:03:00.209
something rarely seen in big-screen blockbusters.

00:03:00.209 --> 00:03:04.209
Black Panther marks the first time a black
superhero is leading a movie in the modern

00:03:04.209 --> 00:03:09.080
MCU, and it's also an important milestone
behind the camera, with Ryan Coogler becoming

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.600
the first black director of a Marvel movie.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:15.659
This was reflected in the movie's audience
— according to The Hollywood Reporter, 37

00:03:15.659 --> 00:03:19.470
percent of the opening weekend audience for
the movie was African-American, compared to

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:22.530
an average of 15 percent for other superhero
films.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:23.720
Disney's Dave Hollis said,

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:27.999
"Our goal is to make movies that reflect the
diversity of our world because those are the

00:03:27.999 --> 00:03:29.880
stories that resonate everywhere.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:33.920
To have the ability to show other people's
experience is part of the beauty of movies,

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:38.190
but it also allows for rich storytelling,
and for the people whose experiences are up

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:41.329
on the screen, especially if they have not
been showcased a ton."

00:03:41.329 --> 00:03:42.329
[...]

00:03:42.329 --> 00:03:45.560
"The meaningful nature of being able to see
yourself represented, those things really

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:50.409
matter to everyone, but in this case it matters
even more to communities of color.

00:03:50.409 --> 00:03:54.120
Representation matters and the times we've
leaned into it, we've had massive results."

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.340
#WhatBlackPantherMeansToMe

00:03:55.340 --> 00:04:01.250
Black Panther has a special place in the hearts
of many viewers, and they took to social media

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:06.500
with the hashtag #WhatBlackPantherMeansToMe
to express their enthusiasm about the movie.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:10.700
The hashtag was created by Kayla Sutton, the
director of online marketing for Black Girl

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:13.750
Nerds, and was inspired by her 8-year-old
son.

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:14.900
One Twitter user wrote,

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:19.530
"It means that my kids and young black kids
everywhere will see themselves as heroes capable

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:20.970
of leading their own narratives."

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:22.610
...while another said that the movie meant

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:23.990
"Everything.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:25.520
I cried when it was announced.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:26.840
I cried at the visuals.

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:29.520
I cried at the #SDCC Marvel booth.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.060
I cried in joy.

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:32.590
Their blackness is mine.

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:34.240
My blackness is theirs.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:38.830
Black Panther is a love letter, a celebration,
and a victory march for the diaspora."

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:43.910
The outpouring on social media helped to build
even more buzz for the movie, and helped solidify

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:46.780
its place as a cultural milestone.

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:48.449
Strong female characters

00:04:48.449 --> 00:04:53.030
Black Panther also received a lot of praise
for its strong female characters, led by Lupita

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:59.800
Nyong'o's Nakia, Danai Gurira's Okoye, Letitia
Wright's Shuri, and Angela Bassett's Ramonda.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:04.330
As was the case with the 2017 box office hit
Wonder Woman, female audiences turned out

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:08.960
in full force to support these powerful ladies
— 45 percent of the opening weekend viewers

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:13.300
were women, compared to 35 to 40 percent for
most superhero movies.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:17.900
The movie's badass women also got a lot of
attention on social media, with one tweet

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:22.789
calling Shuri "the Disney Princess I've been
waiting my whole life for."

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:24.520
No major challengers

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:29.510
Most Marvel movies don't face huge competition,
as other studios avoid scheduling movies opposite

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:32.000
Marvel's many blockbuster juggernauts.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:37.259
And Black Panther was no exception, as it
faced almost no competition from minor new

00:05:37.259 --> 00:05:39.080
releases Early Man and Samson.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:43.949
And the forecast looks good as well, as the
next major new release isn't until March 9,

00:05:43.949 --> 00:05:48.250
when Disney drops its next big blockbuster
- A Wrinkle in Time, which also features a

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:50.300
black director and black lead.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:54.780
Looks like Black Panther isn't just king of
Wakanda - he's king of the box office too.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:56.940
Long live the king!

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:57.940
Thanks for watching!

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:00.430
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:02.649
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

